0\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015MINUTES OF A REGULAR MEETING OF\rTHE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF CALABASAS,\rCALIFORNIA, HELD WEDNESDAY, OCTOBER 3, 2007\r\rMayor Bozajian called the meeting to order at 7:30 p.m. in the City Council Chambers of City Hall, 26135 Mureau Road, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Bozajian, Mayor pro Tem Maurer, Councilmembers Groveman, Washburn, Wolfson.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Colantuono, Coroalles, Peirce, Stearns, Tamuri, Yalda.\r\rThe Pledge of Allegiance was led by Viewpoint Students.\r\rAPPROVAL OF AGENDA\r\r Mayor pro Tem Maurer moved, seconded by Councilmember Washburn, to approve the agenda. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rANNOUNCEMENTS/INTRODUCTIONS\r\rMayor pro Tem Maurer recognized everyone who participated in �Walk to School Day� on Wednesday, October 3, 2007. Councilmember Washburn acknowledged those who participated in �Walk to School Day� and spoke regarding Deborah Steller, Julie Talbert and Carol Washburn, who were recognized for the �Women Who Mean Business� Award. He spoke regarding upcoming Halloween events at the City of Calabasas and at Pierce College. Mayor Bozajian spoke regarding the Hidden Hills parade and the Calabasas Pumpkin Festival. Mayor Bozajian and Councilmember Groveman presented proclamations to Viewpoint Students in recognition of their service with disadvantaged youth at the Zeitgeist Center.\r\rORAL COMMUNICATIONS - PUBLIC COMMENT\r\r Ross Hashemi, Calabasas, spoke regarding Alzheimer�s disease and announced that November is National Alzheimer�s Month. Robin Mitchell, Calabasas, spoke regarding restoration and ongoing maintenance of the Sepulveda Adobe.\r\rCONSENT ITEMS \r\r Approval of the minutes for the September 19, 2007 City Council meeting. \r\r Recommendation to accept completion of the Mulholland Highway Roadway Improvements, Project Specification No. 06-07-09, by Nye and Nelson Inc.; and to direct the City Clerk to file the Notice of Completion. \r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2007-1104, to accept and authorize staff to transfer the maintenance of the Sanitary Sewer Improvements for New Millennium Homes, Inc. Tract 35596 Phases 01-05, Private Contract 00-01, to Los Angeles County Sewer Maintenance District of the State of California. \r\rCouncilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Councilmember Washburn, to approve Consent Item #1, 2, and 3. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rUNFINISHED BUSINESS\r\r Discussion regarding an ordinance restricting smoking in multi-family rental housing.\r\r\r\rCharles and Lisa Wintner, Calabasas, Esther Schiller, Smoke-free Air for Everyone, Dr. Thomas Pfeffer, American Heart Association and Kaiser Permanente, Karina Arabolaza, Housing Rights Center, Amanda Martin, Calabasas, Ross Hashemi, Michelle Hashemi, Calabasas, Alan Zopar, William McCarthy, Department of Public Health, University of California Los Angeles, Patrick Reynolds, Foundation for a Smoke-free America, Alisha Lopez, Tobacco Free Los Angeles, Marlene Gomez, Smoke-free Air for Everyone, Steven Gallegos, American Lung Association of California, Jack Nicholl, State Board of the American Lung Association, Fatemeh Jabari, Calabasas, Matthew Karedas, Calabasas, Edmy Figuera, Oxnard, Sam Savoia, Calabasas, spoke in support of the City adopting an ordinance restricting smoking in multi-family rental housing. Mark Shear, Calabasas, Alissa Rich, Calabasas, Jenny Rich, Calabasas, Janice Gelgood, Agoura Hills, spoke in opposition to adopting an ordinance restricting smoking in multi-family rental housing.\r\rThe City Council provided direction for the continued drafting of a proposed ordinance restricting smoking in multi-family rental housing.\r\rThe City Council recessed at 9:20 p.m. and reconvened at 9:35 p.m.\r\rNEW BUSINESS\r\r Discussion regarding development of an historic preservation ordinance.\r\rGeoff Stearns, Senior Planner, presented the staff report. \r\rDebbie Bruschaber, Oak Park, President of the Calabasas Historic Society, Robin Mitchell, Calabasas, spoke in support of an historic preservation ordinance.\r\rThe City Council provided direction to staff on the proposed historic preservation ordinance.\r\rINFORMATIONAL REPORTS\r\r Check Register for the period of September 12, 2007 to September 20, 2007.\r\r There was no action taken.\r\rTASK FORCE REPORTS\r\r Councilmember Washburn announced that the Civic Center Task Force will be meeting on October 9, 2007.\r\rCITY MANAGER�S REPORT\r\r City Manager Coroalles indicated that he had nothing to report.\r\rFUTURE AGENDA ITEMS\r\r Mayor pro Tem Maurer announced that and Education Fund meeting and the return of the ordinance restricting smoking in multi-family rental housing will be scheduled for the meeting of November 28, 2007.\r\rADJOURN\r\rThe City Council adjourned at 10:30 p.m. in memory of Leonard Kishimoto.\r\r\r\r\r______________________________\rRobin Parker, City Clerk\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0013PAGE \u0014- 2 -\u0015\r\r\r\u0013 PAGE \\* MERGEFORMAT \u00142\u0015\r10/03/07\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u000